			"notes": "## Aller Client 1.1.0\n\nA large new update. Sixteen new HUD elements, a set of inventory tools, photo mode, an in-game updater, and a pocket dimension you can now share with friends.\n\n### New HUD elements\n\n- **Looking at**, **held item**, **inventory view** and **free slots**\n- **Cooldowns**, **elytra flight** and **mount stats**\n- **Experience**, **yaw and pitch**, **session stats** and **pack display**\n- **Server TPS**\n- **Timers**, started from the launcher (`timer 5m`, `stopwatch`). They ring whether or not the HUD element is on.\n- **Now playing**, read from the Windows media controls (Windows only)\n- **Durability warnings**, plus a tint for low health or hunger\n\n### Inventory and items\n\nInventory and container screens stay vanilla. These draw on top of them:\n\n- **Inventory search**: press Ctrl+F or click the button above the inventory.\n- **Container preview**: hover a shulker box to see what is inside.\n- **Item details** and **enchantment notes** in tooltips.\n- **Item lock**: protects inventory slots from the drop key.\n- **Chest memory**: remembers what each chest held. \"find\" in the launcher marks matching containers on the HUD. This one is marked restricted, because some servers don't allow it.\n\n### Photo mode\n\nPress **F9** (or use \"Photo mode\" in the launcher). It hides the HUD, and you can turn, roll and zoom the camera on the spot. It has depth of field and colour grading sliders, and it saves a clean picture without the panel. \"Freeze the world\" works in singleplayer.\n\n### Chat bubbles\n\nA bubble appears over a player's head when they speak. It only shows while they are loaded, in range and in line of sight, so it never gives away where someone is.\n\n### Updater\n\nAller Client can now check GitHub for new releases. It looks every ten minutes and can be switched off under \"Check for updates\" in the client settings.\n\n- When a release has a jar for your Minecraft version, a popup on the main menu or pause menu shows its release notes. In a world you get one toast instead.\n- Nothing is downloaded until you press **Update now**. The jar is checked against its size and SHA-256 and against its own `fabric.mod.json`.\n- The game then asks you to close it, and the old jar is deleted once it has gone.\n- **What's new** shows once after an update.\n\n### Pocket dimension\n\n- **Host the pocket** turns it into a normal singleplayer world that friends can join through Open to LAN, Essential or e4mc.\n- **Back to the server** saves and closes it, then rejoins the multiplayer server you came from.\n\nThe pocket is still experimental, restricted and off by default.\n\n### Other mods' menu buttons\n\nMods such as Flashback add buttons to Minecraft's title and pause screens, which Aller Client replaces. Those buttons now collect in a drawer below the Essential strip.\n\n- Pin a row to give it its own button, and right-click that button to unpin it.\n- Hide a row you don't want.\n- A master switch in the UI settings turns the whole thing off.\n\n### Fixes\n\n- The smooth camera no longer gets stuck on after zooming.\n\n### Downloads\n\nTake the jar for your Minecraft version: `aller-1.1.0+26.2.jar` or `aller-1.1.0+1.21.8.jar`. The updater matches on that file name, so don't rename it."
		},
